  title: Religion in the Gupta age
  text: Gupta kings were mainly devotees of Vishnu, and Puranic Hinduism with temple worship grew. Buddhism and Jainism also flourished; the great monastery of Nalanda was founded in the 5th century under Kumaragupta.
